# Line endings are not cosmetic in this repository.
#
# The local sink is byte-preserving on purpose (internal/sink) so the evidence chain built from
# these messages downstream stays verifiable, and that chain hashes canonical bytes. Git's default
# on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout, which changes those bytes and
# does so differently depending on who cloned the repo and on what OS.
#
# These are marked as non-text so git performs NO conversion in either direction: whatever bytes are
# committed are the bytes on disk, on every machine. Deliberately a freeze rather than a
# normalisation -- the fixtures already in this repository carry CRLF, and rewriting them to LF
# would change the exact bytes the tests were verified against, which is the thing this file exists
# to prevent.
*.ndjson -text
*.jsonl  -text

# Not text at all.
*.exe    binary
*.png    binary
